# ~/.claude is a live runtime directory that holds SECRETS and full session
# transcripts. This file is therefore an ALLOWLIST, not a blocklist:
#
#   1. ignore everything
#   2. re-admit only the specific config paths we intend to publish
#
# Written this way on purpose. A blocklist would mean that any secret file a
# future Claude Code version drops in here gets committed until someone notices.
# With an allowlist, anything new is excluded by default and has to be admitted
# deliberately.
#
# NEVER re-admit: credentials.json, .credentials.json (Claude auth),
# history.jsonl, projects/ (session transcripts + per-machine memory),
# sessions/, tasks/, jobs/, keystores/, session-env/, paste-cache/, debug/,
# daemon.log, shell-snapshots/, file-history/.

# 1. Ignore everything.
*

# 2. Re-admit the config we publish. Directories need both the dir and its
#    contents un-ignored, hence the /** entries.
!.gitignore
!README.md
!CLAUDE.md
!settings.json

!commands/
!commands/**

!agents/
!agents/**

!skills/
!skills/**

!hooks/
!hooks/**

!tools/
!tools/**

# 3. Belt and braces: even if a path above is widened later, these can never be
#    committed. Order matters — these come after the re-admissions.
credentials.json
.credentials.json
*.key
*.pem
*.pfx
*secret*
*token*
settings.local.json
